        <p>As several of our readers have suggested a Solving Tourney, we on November sth commenced one. We shall give a cash prize of 53. per month to the reader who succeeds in placing himself at the head of the solvers' list at the end of each calendar month. If two or more competitors tie for the first place, the prize will be ballotted for. The winner's score will then be cancelled, the re- maining competitors' points going towards the next month's competition. The winner rr,ay re.enter the tourney, commenc- ing again at the bottom of the list. Points will be awarded as follows: Two points for the correct solution of a problem ; two points for correcting the author's terms ; two points for showing a dual solution ; and one point for each minor correction. Intending competitors may enter at any time. PROFS GEM. CO MP ETITION. We alsl offer a cash prize of 23 6d., for the best original Problem sent in during the month of November. The deci-lon of the Draughts E litor to be flint in this and the solving tourney.</p>
