        <p>....---,_... eiROSSLEY'S 12 h.p. GA S ENGINE; first-elasa order; 1.../ seen running ; replacing by steam; all Rttinxe complete Particulara,ELOLMES,Surrey Lodge, Crewe.</p>
        <p>pITTS'S MANCHESTERISpeaking of this well-known firm, 1 "The South Manchester Chronicle"of 0ct.7,1898. says'— "There, in a palatial five-storey building having a capacity of over 1.000,04 feet and magnificent show windows over 250 feet long,can be found every article required for the se la- tic and economical furnishing of mansion, villa, or cottage that the most fastidious connoisseur could desire, and al- though the premises are so fast and the magnitude and mid- tipliuity of the stock so great, still everything, including electric light throughout, passenger lifts to all floors, 15 Si well planned and so conveniently arranged that inspection becomes quite a pleasure. Whether your house be £2O or £220 per annum, a very short space of time will suffice in which to select every necessary article for its furnishing throughout in a comfortable and durable evsn luxurious manner, whilst paying due regard to economical considera- tions. No person not having visited Pitts's could possibly conceive Id e immense variety of their well selected stock, and the astonishingly low prices quoted can only be explained on the ground that the management being large purchasers for cash evidently buy in the very best market directly from the actual manufacturers, thus obviating all intermediate profits. The firm is well reputed and old established, having been founded over half a century ago by the present proprie- tor, Samuel Pitts, who still personally presides over its des- tinies, ably seconded by members of his family, bred and I born in the trade, and a competent and painstaking staff individuals of which have been in his employ from 10 to 20 years. It was started in an exceedingly humble way, and has only reached its present colossal proportions by dint of sound judgment, untiring energy, and never flagging enter- prise. In short, we have unbounded confidence in strongly recommending this very estimable establishment to all about to furnish, whether in part or throughout, feeling convinced that by so doing we are rendering a very valuable service to our numerous readers, and bestowing just and well-merited praise were due. ' Pfilmam qui meruit ferat."</p>
        <p>I 1101ITTS'S are constantly receiving similar Press Opinions to the above, all expressing UNQUALIFIED PRAISE 'of PITTS'S unrivalled PREMISES, STOCK, and BUSINESS METHODS. This is extremely gratifying to PITTS'S and will spur them on to still further efforts to supply the public with REALLY RELIABLE ARTICLES at VERY LOWEST PRICES. Undoubtedly it is the BOUNDEN DUTY of every- one desirous of obtaining UTMOST POSSIBLE VALUE to give us a call before deciviing.</p>
        <p>PITTEPS FOR CARPETS AND FLOOR COVRRINGS.— All British made. Largest. best, and cheapest stock. Astounding value. Grandest disp:ay ever seen.</p>
        <p>PITTS S CYCLES, BASSINETTBS, Lamps, China, Glass, Earthenware, Magnificent display in Show Windows. Guaranteed Great Saving.</p>
        <p>CORPORATION OF THE CITY OF MAg CHICSTER. CONCENTRATED MANURE Made from Slaughter-house and Market Refuse, Excrement from Pail Closets, BLOOD, BObi ES, FISH, &amp;a., Delivered in bags, carriage paid, in 2 Ton lots within 60 miles and 4 Ton lots within 100 miles, at +.1.3 per Ton. Supply strictly limited. Orders should be given early In the season to prevent dis‘ppolntment. Full particulars:from R. D. CALLISON, Indoor andoEstates Super- intendent, Cleansing Department, Town Hall, Manchester. Or to Mr. B. ALDRED, Stamford-rd., Altrinoliam. Mr. J. H. NEWTON, West Derby, Liverpool, Mr. J. S. GA.LLisin, Brookflelds, Baddiley. near lsiantwich.</p>
