      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1898-11-18_WidnesExaminer_art0082" n="art0082">
        <head>EXAMINER, FRIDAY, NOVEMBER 18, 1898.</head>
        <p>THE EXAMINER, FRIDAY, NOVEMBER 18, 1898.</p>
        <p>one of the posts, whence it rebounded into play. Im- mediately the ball was dropped out Walker dribblet/ to the Salford goal hue, and Nickson gaining possession ran in another try, and Farmer placed a goal. This placed the teams on level terms—tsn paints each,—a change in the aspect of the game the Salford support?rs could hardly realise. The prospect of a keen struggle for vic- toay was, however,soon rendered improbabl: by Hough- I ton twisting his knee, and being compelled, after resuming play for a saort time, to retire from the game. Warder took his place, and a fairly good effort was made by the visitors to save We match, but they failed to do so, 11.. skins, after fine passing by his collcagues,securing an unconverted try for Salford. Pearson ale) had a fair opening, but kicked to) hard, and Poillips failed to I place a penalty from an easy position in front of the Ron- corn posts. Result :—Salford, two goals and three tries (thirteen points) ; Runcorn, two goals and two tries (ten points.)</p>
