        <p>3ln. H. W. SETON-RAR—R IN SEARCH OF THE GARDEN OF EDEN. On Tuesday a small scientific party left Aden on an expedition of peculiar interest. Its object is discover the exact locality of tha Garden of Eden . The expedition, which i 3 under the direction of Mr., 11. W. Seton-Karr, the well-known traveller, ex plorer and hunter, is making for the Palmolithi settlement in Somalilonl,which is thought to cove the supposed site. Mr. Seton-Karr has alread made several discoveries of archasrlogical and per-, ' logical importance,and from his examination of the whole district, has come to the conclusion that itS features entirely corresponl with this° described in Genesis. He is not even troubled with the vexed question of the four rivers, for which he has many plausible solution.</p>
